<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gyebaek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 660</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gyebaek was a general of the Korean kingdom of Baekje. In 660, as Silla and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> invaded, he led a small army against a much larger Silla force at Hwangsanbeol; according to tradition he first killed his own family so that they would not be enslaved. He won several engagements before he was killed and his army destroyed, and he is remembered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> as a model of loyalty.</p></div>
